<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Sultan ibn Saif</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">r. <a href="/years/1649">1649</a>–<a href="/years/1688">1688</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/17th-century">17th century</a> · Also known as Sultan bin Saif I</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc"><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sultan">Sultan</a> ibn Saif was <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/imam">imam</a> of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/oman">Oman</a> of the Ya'aruba dynasty from 1649 to 1688. In 1650 he captured <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/muscat">Muscat</a>, ending Portuguese rule on the Omani coast, and built a navy that attacked Portuguese posts in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/india">India</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/east-africa">East Africa</a>, beginning Oman's rise as a maritime power. He also built the great round fort at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nizwa">Nizwa</a>.</p></div>
